7. Submitted homework

   (a) Review license. By submitting your homework (a repository or a ZIP),
       you grant the Licensor, and the instructors and reviewers acting on the
       Licensor's behalf to deliver the Bootcamp, a non-exclusive,
       royalty-free license to use your submission as needed to deliver the
       Bootcamp and its review service, namely to:
         (i)    access and review the submitted repository or ZIP;
         (ii)   copy it into a private review environment;
         (iii)  import its World into the private Superwork Studio;
         (iv)   validate, execute, test, simulate, inspect and analyze the
                submitted World and scenarios;
         (v)    display and discuss the submission with you during feedback
                and 1:1 review sessions;
         (vi)   make the temporary technical copies necessary for these
                activities; and
         (vii)  provide feedback and suggested modifications.

   (b) De-identified learnings. You also grant the Licensor a non-exclusive,
       perpetual, royalty-free right, after de-identifying, normalizing,
       aggregating or generalizing a submission so that the resulting material
       does not identify, and is not reasonably capable of being used to
       identify, the participant, the participant's employer, any client or
       any individual, to derive from it patterns, structures, examples,
       statistics and learnings, and to use them for Superwork product
       improvement, education, research and Superwork Library development.

   (c) Limits. These permissions do not transfer ownership of your original
       Participant Work. They do not include a right to publicly redistribute
       your raw submission.

   (d) Your content. Submit only material you are allowed to share. Do not
       include confidential information, personal data, credentials or
       secrets (see the README's sensitive-information warning).

